message.content:
{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be helping take care of you during this hospital stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:42:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been feeling really off. I had diarrhea for a few days, but that stopped last night. Now I have a headache, dizziness, and pain in my left lower belly. Also, my feet hurt—like a burning and itching feeling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:43:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And I understand you’ve been having some other symptoms—your daughter mentioned hallucinations?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:44:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, just a little—like shadows moving. I was worried. And I’ve been tired, with no appetite, just feel full all the time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:45:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. You’ve had a kidney transplant recently, and you’re on several medications, including Prograf. Your level came back very high—23—so you were told to hold a dose. That might be contributing to how you’re feeling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:46:35",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, so that could be why I’m dizzy and seeing things? I was scared it was something serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:47:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible. High Prograf levels can affect the brain. We’ve lowered your dose to 3mg twice a day for now, and we’ll check it again tomorrow. That should help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:48:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. But what about the belly pain? It’s near my JP drain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:49:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We examined you—the area is red and warm, tracking from the drain site. That suggests cellulitis, a skin infection. We’ll start antibiotics for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:50:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had that before, after my hernia surgery. Is it MRSA again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t think so this time. We’re starting doxycycline, which covers common skin bacteria. We’ll monitor how it improves."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:52:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my urine test showed an infection too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:53:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you have a UTI caused by E. coli. It’s resistant to some antibiotics, so we started IV ceftriaxone. Once we know the best oral option, we’ll switch you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:54:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad we caught it. I didn’t even have burning or urgency."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:55:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common with transplant patients—your symptoms can be subtle. We’re also watching your kidney function. Your creatinine is up a bit, but we think it’s due to the infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:56:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my feet? The redness and pain—is that related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:57:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed the redness on the soles. It could be related to circulation or a side effect of medications. We’ll keep an eye on it. For now, we don’t think it’s an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:58:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. And my JP drain—output is down to 20ml a day. Should we remove it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2155-11-21 12:59:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good sign—low output means it’s ready to come out. The urology team will remove your ureteral stent tomorrow, and we’ll assess the drain then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2155-11-21 13:00:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. I just want to feel like myself again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2155-11-22 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood cultures came back clean—no bacteria in the blood. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2155-11-22 08:16:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. How’s the UTI looking?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2155-11-22 08:17:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sensitivity testing showed the E. coli is sensitive to cefpodoxime. We’ll switch you to that oral antibiotic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2155-11-22 08:18:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the stent removal—is that today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2155-11-22 08:19:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, later this morning. It’s a quick procedure at the bedside. It might help with your flank and belly discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2155-11-22 08:20:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope so. The pain’s been nagging."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2155-11-22 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The stent is out. You did great. Any pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2155-11-22 12:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just a little sore, but much better than before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2155-11-22 12:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep you on doxycycline for the cellulitis and switch to cefpodoxime for the UTI. Your Prograf level this morning was 11.1—much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2155-11-22 12:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go back to my regular dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2155-11-22 12:34:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We’ll keep it at 3mg twice a day for now. The transplant team will call you tonight with long-term adjustments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2155-11-22 12:35:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my INR? I’m on Coumadin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2155-11-22 12:36:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s stable. You’ll take 1mg tonight, and they’ll check it again tomorrow to guide your next dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2155-11-23 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re looking better. The redness around your abdomen is improving, and you’re afebrile."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2155-11-23 08:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel better. Headache’s gone, and I’m eating a little more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2155-11-23 08:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Your labs show improvement—creatinine is down to 3.1, and white count is normalizing. We’ll plan for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2155-11-23 08:03:35",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. What meds will I go home on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2155-11-23 08:04:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue mycophenolate, valganciclovir, levothyroxine, and metoprolol. Omeprazole is now 20mg twice a day. And you’ll take doxycycline for 7 days and cefpodoxime for 12."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2155-11-23 08:06:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And Prograf?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2155-11-23 08:06:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue 3mg twice a day until the transplant team calls with further instructions. They’ll call you tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2155-11-23 08:07:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the drain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2155-11-23 08:08:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Output is low—20ml/day—so we’ll remove it before you go home. We’ll give you instructions on how to care for the site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2155-11-23 08:09:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my feet? Still a little red."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2155-11-23 08:10:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think it’s related to circulation or medication. It’s not spreading, so we’ll monitor it as an outpatient. Wear comfortable shoes and report any worsening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2155-11-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home. The drain is out, and you’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2155-11-24 09:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. What should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2155-11-24 09:02:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call the transplant clinic if you have fever, chills, nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea. Watch the incision for redness, drainage, or bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2155-11-24 09:03:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2155-11-24 09:04:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get a full list. Take cefpodoxime daily for 12 days, doxycycline every 12 hours for 7. The transplant team will call tonight about your Prograf. Take only 1mg of Coumadin tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2155-11-24 09:05:35",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll wait for their call. Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2155-11-24 09:06:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You’ve made great progress. Rest, follow up, and we’ll see you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2155-11-24 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2155-11-24 10:31:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. Ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2155-11-24 10:32:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Remember, home health will draw your Prograf level and INR tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2155-11-24 10:33:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I have it scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2155-11-24 10:34:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. Keep taking your meds as directed and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2155-11-24 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your discharge paperwork is ready. You’re cleared to leave whenever you’re ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2155-11-24 11:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I feel much safer going home now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2155-11-24 11:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad we could help. Take care, and don’t hesitate to call."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2155-11-24 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you’re all set to go? Transportation is here?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2155-11-24 13:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, my daughter’s outside. Thank you again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2155-11-24 13:02:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Stay well, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2155-11-24 13:03:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Take care!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2155-11-24 13:04:55",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2155-11-24 13:06:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2155-11-24 13:07:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it easy and rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2155-11-24 13:08:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Goodbye!"
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2155-11-21 12:41:00",
    "admission_end": "2155-11-24 13:46:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with symptoms of a urinary tract infection, left lower quadrant pain, headache, dizziness, and hallucinations. She had recently been discharged after a kidney transplant and was found to have a supratherapeutic tacrolimus level of 23, which was adjusted to 3mg twice daily, leading to clinical improvement. She was diagnosed with an E. coli UTI resistant to ampicillin and ciprofloxacin, treated initially with ceftriaxone and later transitioned to oral cefpodoxime. Abdominal cellulitis near her JP drain site was treated with doxycycline, with visible improvement. Her ureteral stent was removed on hospital day 2, and the JP drain was discontinued prior to discharge. She was discharged home in good condition with instructions to continue antibiotics, adjust anticoagulation with warfarin, and await further tacrolimus dosing guidance from the transplant team.",
    "problems": [
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Cellulitis and abscess of trunk",
      "Escherichia coli [E. coli] infection in conditions classified elsewhere and of unspecified site",
      "Kidney replaced by transplant",
      "Other postoperative infection",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of other parts of uterus",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Hyperparathyroidism, unspecified",
      "Surgical operation with transplant of whole organ causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation"
    ]
  }
}
